This '''species''' was a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="ROTS" />

==Biology and appearance==
This bipedal [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] was distinguished primarily by their pointed [[ear]]s.<ref name="ROTS" />

==Species in the galaxy==
By [[19 BBY]],<ref name="SWGA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> a member of this species had been remembered as one of the [[Four Masters]], founders the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> They were depicted via one of four massive sculptures that overlooked the [[Processional Way]] leading in to the Temple up until the [[Great Jedi Purge|fall of the Jedi Order]].<ref name="ROTS" />

==Behind the scenes==
This species first appeared in the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], directed by [[George Lucas]].<ref name="ROTS" /> The Four Masters were originally designed by [[Aaron McBride]] and [[Ryan Church]] under the direction of Lucas between October and December [[2003]], but were depicted as different species and in different postures<ref name="Art of ROTS">''[[The Art of Revenge of the Sith]]''</ref> than in the final film.<ref name="ROTS" /> For their appearance in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]] of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' they were worked on by [[Chris Glenn]] and [[Kilian Plunkett]].<ref name="TCW Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/sabotage-episode-guide|text="Sabotage" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

